Weight terms are separate from this MIT file.

LoRA adapters and their sources
-------------------------------

The LoRA adapters distributed with BonJev (work/best/, and the Hugging Face
adapter repositories) are training-free recombinations of third-party decision
LoRA deltas. The source models are all Apache-2.0, so the resulting adapters are
distributed under the Apache License 2.0 as well; the sources are listed, with
licenses and notices, in docs/ATTRIBUTION.md.

Sources in the published adapters (all Apache-2.0):
  lostargon/Tiny-Jev, jaredpalmer/kev-4b, CullenYap/CandiGate-Qwen3-4B,
  sennaLLMLearner/qwen3-4b-system-one-lora, jaredpalmer/kev-8b,
  CaoHaoWei/Jev-LCT-Qwen3-8B, Cloudflare/clef,
  totum-labs/Qwen3.5-27B-plumb, vllm-sr/Decision-2.0-Vega-27B.

Sources used in experiments and all base models are Apache-2.0; the full list is
in docs/ATTRIBUTION.md.

Considered but not used, and therefore not in any adapter:
  HopitAI/hopper (research and demo use only),
  dhtocks/malkuth-4b (CC-BY-NC-4.0, non-commercial).
